list.item:
Goods consigned from any country. This list includes products for
                            which import control is either impracticable or undesirable, and of
                            little trade importance, such as fresh shell fish (other than frozen);
                            books and periodicals in single copies sent through the mails; seaweed;
                            ivory (animal); architectural or engineering designs; press photographs;
                            newspapers; exposed cinematograph films; hydrographic charts; maps and
                            plans; gold bullion and coin, and gold ores, concentrates, and
                            residues.
